{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cloud Computing Service Agreements"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about different cloud computing services."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.   Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Was/were supposed to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In order to express an assumption in the past, we can use the structure <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\"> was/were supposed to. </span> </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we talk about things that should have happened in the past or should have been done, we can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> be supposed to</span></span> in its past form is used to say that something was expected to happen but never did. </br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Subject + was/were + supposed to + verb base form + complement</span></br></br>  \u2022\t<span class=\"italic\">Both parties <span class=\"strong\">were supposed to come</span> to an agreement, but finally they didn't.\t</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Actually, the proposal submission deadline was supposed to be yesterday."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A few years ago, you were supposed to just accept the terms."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In the past, you were supposed to be granted a software license."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of modal verbs, can"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <strong>passive voice</strong> when we want to give importance to the object of a sentence or when the subject is unknown or not important."}, {"type": "text", "content": " We can use the passive voice with the modal verb <strong>can</strong> to talk about present ability or possibility. Its doer is unknown or is not important. </br></br> \t To make the passive with <strong>can</strong>, the <strong>to be</strong> verb is used in its base form, followed by the main verb in its past participle form: </br></br>  \u2022\t<i>Specific conditions <strong>can be laid out</strong> in a contract proposal before both parties start to negotiate. </i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How do you think these proposals can be approached?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We should consider if free cloud services that can be offered to thousands of users fit better than cloud services which are tailored to a few customers. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "A cloud service is a time-based subscription that can be ended according to the customer's satisfaction."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "submission"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something which is offered so that it can be chosen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Actually, the proposal submission deadline was supposed to be yesterday. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to adapt properly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We should consider if free cloud services that can be offered to thousands of users fit better than cloud services which are tailored to a few customers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "moreover"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in addition "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Moreover, paid cloud services vendors provide customized services, a 24/7 customer service, and avoid an outage at all costs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "differ"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be different "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now, how do cloud computing service contracts differ from a traditional software purchase?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to agree to give"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the past, you were supposed to be granted a software license."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "everlasting "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that lasts forever, or for a long time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the traditional software model, the client pays upfront for an everlasting license."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a broader research about cloud  computing services."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss with a partner your findings and from your experience using cloud services. What advantages and disadvantages do you find from this service? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a 250 words report expressing your final thoughts and mentioning at least three advantages and disadvantages of cloud services."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can make a broader research about cloud computing services."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can discuss and share ideas with a partner about cloud services pros and cons."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can write a 250 words report expressing my final thoughts about the topic for discussion."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le01ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Mark</strong>: Have we received any interesting proposals from cloud services vendors? </br>\n<strong>Walter</strong>: We have. Actually, the proposal submission deadline was supposed to be yesterday. </br>\n<strong>Mark</strong>: Good! How do you think these proposals can be approached? </br>\n<strong>Walter</strong>: It depends on if it's a paid, a free, or a low-cost cloud service. We should consider if free cloud services that can be offered to thousands of users fit better than cloud services which are tailored to a few customers. Moreover, paid cloud services vendors provide customized services, a 24/7 customer service, and avoid an outage at all costs. Also, now paid cloud contracts are open for negotiation. A few years ago, you were supposed to just accept the terms."}, {"time": "51000", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Mark</strong>: Good observation. Now, how do cloud computing service contracts differ from a traditional software purchase? </br>\n<strong>Walter</strong>: In the past, you were supposed to be granted a software license. Now, the software code belongs to the cloud vendor, so there's no clause stating \"vendor hereby grants a license to a customer to copy and use the software\" as in a traditional contract. Additionally, in the traditional software model, the client pays upfront for an everlasting license, whereas a cloud service is a time-based subscription that can be ended according to the customer's satisfaction."}, {"time": "94000", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Mark</strong>: How will the security and privacy of our data be kept in cloud computer services? </br>\n<strong>Walter</strong>: Cloud vendors probably won't guarantee data security for the price of a subscription, but they do offer practical and contractual assurances. They would somehow state their reasonable determination and efforts to protect customers' data. In addition, there should be contractual statements on how the vendor is expected to manage the data and the retrieval of data upon termination of the contract by the customer."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le01ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the differences between paid and free clouding services. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss how cloud computing service contracts differ from a traditional software purchase."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about practical and contractual assurances to keep the security and privacy of a customer's data."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do 